  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed conversion would result in the loss of a 3-bedroom family dwelling and fails to provide adequate compensatory family accommodation, leading to a net reduction in family housing within the borough. This outcome undermines the Council's strategic objective to increase the supply of larger (3+ bedroom) units, which are essential to meeting the housing needs of families. The proposal is therefore contrary to National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policy GG4 of the London Plan (2021), Policy CP5 of the Core Strategy (2010), Policies DMD4 and DMD5 of the Development Management Document (2014).",
    "The proposed development, by reason of the lack of private amenity space most notably for the first floor flat, would result in a substandard form of accommodation that would be detrimental to the residential amenities of future occupants. The proposal is therefore contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policy D6 of the London Plan (2021), Policy CP4 and CP5 of the Enfield Plan Core Strategy (2010), Policies DMD5 and DMD9 of the Development Management Document (2014).",
    "The proposed roof terrace by reason of its siting, size and relationship with neighbouring properties, would be at an elevated vantage point offering direct unobstructed panoramic views towards the adjoining rear gardens of adjoining properties. This would cause an unacceptable level of actual and perceived overlooking and undue loss of privacy to private amenity space as well as an unacceptable increased level of noise and disturbance for the neighbouring properties. As such, it constitutes an unneighbourly form of development and the proposal is contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF, 2024), Policy D3 of the London Plan (2021), DMD 8, DMD9 and DMD68 of the Development Management Document (2014) and Policy CP30 of the Core Strategy (2010).\r\r",
    "The proposed terrace by virtue of its design, materials, scale, siting, and projection would represent an awkward and incongruous addition which would fail to relate to the existing dwelling and the surrounding character, form, and pattern of development contrary to policies DMD13 and DMD37 of the Development Management Document (2014), CP30 of the Core Strategy (2010) and D3 of the London Plan (2021) and National Planning Policy Framework (2024)."
  ],
